YAAD:  Seven years bad luck, or just until you get killed, whichever
comes first.

My latest barbarian suffered a slow, painful, and most definitely
annoying death.

Eating a hill orc corpse won me a nasty case of food poisoning.  This,
I don't entirely understand.  I could have sworn that corpse was not
three turns old.  Is there any chance of a "fresh" corpse giving food
poisoning?  More likely, I just wasn't paying enough attention.

Anyway, my first impulse, lacking a unicorn horn, was to pray to Set.
Unfortunately, I had made the mistake of killing a nymph with a wand
of striking not a dozen turns earlier, breaking the mirror she was
carrying.  I did not fully understand how nasty that -2 luck penalty
could be, or how negative luck affected prayer.  Obviously, Set was
not being very helpful.

So, not knowing its B/U/C status, I whip out my recently purchased
magic lamp and start rubbing furiously.  Lucky me, I get to wish for a
blessed unicorn horn.  Unlucky me, it gets generated cursed (I assume,
once again, due to my breaking that mirror).

I had a potion in my inventory that price ID'ing had indicated MIGHT
be full healing, so I quaff it.  I know this works against sickness,
but does that include food poisoning?.  Anyway, it turns out to be
speed, no help there.

In desperation, I read a scroll of teleport, hoping it will get me
close enough to the general store to quaff any usefull potions the
shop is carrying before the poison kills me. But, the cursed unicorn
horn had managed to get me confused  before I realized it was cursed.
I end up level teleporting three levels down, with little else to do
but wait to die.

*Sigh* Here I go again...

